Sit down.

271
00:29:11,880 --> 00:29:13,479
Sit down..

272
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:17,359
...Karesi Bey.

273
00:29:29,680 --> 00:29:31,399
Enjoy.

274
00:29:33,320 --> 00:29:34,999
Thank you.

275
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:37,519
You didn't have to.

276
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:40,199
Enjoy.

277
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:46,159
But...

278
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,919
...for us...

279
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:52,879
...there is nothing more
important than the sacred relics.

280
00:29:55,440 --> 00:29:57,519
I'm listening to you.

281
00:29:58,480 --> 00:29:59,959
I came to you.

282
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:03,719
And said..

283
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:06,349
...let's look for the
sacred relics together.

284
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:07,639
But...

285
00:30:11,120 --> 00:30:14,169
...Karesi Bey disagreed to work together.

286
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,559
I said okay.

287
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:20,399
I said okay.

288
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:21,999
Then...

289
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:25,029
...I thought I'd look for them alone.

290
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:28,639
But every move I made...

291
00:30:30,520 --> 00:30:33,279
Karesi Bey tried to
stop every move I made.

292
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:38,759
Hear what you're saying first.

293
00:30:39,200 --> 00:30:42,239
-This is an accusation.
-It is not.

294
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:44,359
It's the truth.

295
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:46,679
What are you saying Osman Bey?

296
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:49,879
Whatever you heard is
the truth, Hadrath Vizier.

297
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,959
Karesi Bey...

298
00:30:53,120 --> 00:30:56,279
...sent his alps after me.

299
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:04,399
He made sure the monk I
caught to find the relics died.

300
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:07,719
Karesi Bey...

301
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:10,599
What he was after...

302
00:31:11,560 --> 00:31:14,039
...wasn't the relics.

303
00:31:15,360 --> 00:31:17,799
It was his own ambition.

304
00:31:19,440 --> 00:31:22,519
So your fight for your own good...

305
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:25,479
...was greater than the relics!

306
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:31,199
Like you acting this dishonorably
in front of Hadrath Vizier...

307
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:34,159
...wasn't enough...

308
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:35,999
...you also...

309
00:31:36,320 --> 00:31:38,699
...accuse the leader of the Turks...

310
00:31:38,699 --> 00:31:40,879
...me, Karesi Bey.

311
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:45,799
Am I to leave your tents
where I came as a friend...

312
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:49,199
...as foe now?

313
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,599
The path you're leading...

314
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:54,999
...is just a path that leads
to duality and separation.

315
00:31:56,560 --> 00:31:59,039
Rather than your friendship...

316
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:01,239
...your enmity is better.

317
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:05,719
Osman!

318
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:14,439
Your audacity is stepping over the line.

319
00:32:14,440 --> 00:32:16,359
I was born with my audacity.

320
00:32:16,360 --> 00:32:18,839
And my braveness is everlasting.

321
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:23,679
I've always said what I think is
the truth and stand by it like a rock.

322
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:25,359
Come to your senses.

323
00:32:30,880 --> 00:32:32,159
Yes.

324
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:33,679
Osman Bey.

325
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:38,039
You said you have the sacred relics.

326
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:40,759
Where are they?

327
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:54,319
You can't make me marry Arcadeus.

328
00:32:54,320 --> 00:32:56,759
You don't have the right.

329
00:32:58,360 --> 00:33:01,359
Go and take a nice bath, Holofira.

330
00:33:01,360 --> 00:33:02,599
Rest.

331
00:33:02,600 --> 00:33:04,319
Get prettier.

332
00:33:04,640 --> 00:33:06,639
You'll prepare for the wedding.

333
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:12,999
If you force me to marry him...

334
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:15,239
What will you do?

335
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:24,119
I'll kill myself!

336
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:35,959
Holofira.

337
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:49,039
In these lands, if
someone is going to die...

338
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:52,719
...it can only happen by my hand.

339
00:34:06,480 --> 00:34:09,199
This is what you get...

340
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:13,799
...when you don't follow
orders and act on your own.

341
00:34:22,239 --> 00:34:24,559
Karadin is ready...

342
00:34:24,560 --> 00:34:26,319
...for hell just as you ordered.

343
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:28,119
You did well.

344
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:31,359
There is something else.
Begum hatun and his brother.

345
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:35,079
I heard them talking at Karadin.

346
00:34:35,639 --> 00:34:37,159
Cecilia.

347
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:40,459
She was seen while dropping
the poison at Hazal Hatun's tent.

348
00:34:40,459 --> 00:34:42,439
Incompetent fool!

349
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:52,239
Why did you do that?

350
00:34:52,639 --> 00:34:53,799
Why?

351
00:34:53,800 --> 00:34:55,918
The night you went to Kayi tribe...

352
00:34:56,080 --> 00:34:59,439
...she poisoned Osman
Bey's daughter-in-law.

353
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:03,119
Poor woman's baby died.

354
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:08,759
I am going to take her to
Osman Bey with my own hands.

355
00:35:12,480 --> 00:35:13,759
Gonca?

356
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:19,239
Oh Gonca.

357
00:35:23,240 --> 00:35:24,079
Boran.

358
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:44,049
In the name of Allah, the most
merciful, the most beneficent.

359
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:47,559
In the name of Allah, the most
merciful, the most beneficent.

360
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:05,999
Thank Allah.

361
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:08,759
Oh Allah, thank You!

362
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:10,519
Thank You.

363
00:36:23,480 --> 00:36:25,279
Osman Bey.

364
00:36:27,600 --> 00:36:31,479
For the reputation of the Islamic world...

365
00:36:32,480 --> 00:36:34,239
...we kept a secret.

366
00:36:36,720 --> 00:36:39,199
We hid it from you.

367
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:42,919
But you always talked about unity.

368
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:46,039
When you were wanting to be united...

369
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:50,239
...some people acted selfishly...

370
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:55,159
...and tried to stop you.

371
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,519
But...

372
00:37:01,240 --> 00:37:04,079
But you did not give up.

373
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:09,239
You were ready to sacrifice
yourself and your alps.

374
00:37:11,040 --> 00:37:14,799
You saved us from this shame.

375
00:37:17,080 --> 00:37:19,959
Thank you, Osman Bey.

376
00:37:20,560 --> 00:37:23,519
May your state be blessed.

377
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:26,159
Thank you.

378
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:28,479
Thank Allah..

379
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:30,599
...He allowed us to commit good deeds...

380
00:37:32,560 --> 00:37:35,119
...and stop evil.

381
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:42,919
There is always good in the unity...

382
00:37:43,240 --> 00:37:46,679
...of the Muslims, the brotherhood
of Arabs and Turks...

383
00:37:46,960 --> 00:37:53,319
...and their alliance against the evil.

384
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:55,959
You...

385
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:58,119
...proved that...

386
00:37:58,560 --> 00:38:00,919
...to us,
to all of us again.

387
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:05,599
From now on, our Hadrath Caliph...

388
00:38:06,880 --> 00:38:10,199
...will see you as the
guardian of the Islamic world.

389
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:15,079
When I get to Cairo...

390
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:17,079
...I'll send the allegiance.

391
00:38:17,760 --> 00:38:19,359
Thank you, thank you.

392
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:24,759
Send Caliph Hadrath my respects.

393
00:38:24,800 --> 00:38:28,839
We are servers of Allah and the ummah.

394
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:31,759
Thank you Osman Bey.

395
00:38:33,080 --> 00:38:36,359
May you and your state live long.

396
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:42,359
Live long!

397
00:39:31,840 --> 00:39:33,119
What are you doing?

398
00:39:42,680 --> 00:39:43,799
Cecilia.

399
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:47,079
She was guilty.

400
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:48,799
But she was my server.

401
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,799
I wanted to say goodbye.

402
00:39:53,120 --> 00:39:54,239
May she rest in peace.

403
00:39:58,360 --> 00:39:59,439
Don't let her...

404
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:02,999
...ruin our wedding.

405
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:06,199
She was a peasant.

406
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:11,959
I want my bride to be happy.

407
00:40:14,760 --> 00:40:16,399
Don't touch me again.

408
00:40:19,360 --> 00:40:21,279
I'd rather die...

409
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:23,479
..then to marry you.

410
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:34,359
Our love will be a tough one.

411
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:35,999
We're heading out.

412
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:46,959
Let's give Osman Bey what he wants.

413
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:50,479
But first we'll meet Karesi.

414
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:09,679
Kayi Tribe

415
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:19,119
Watch the enemy's
feet as well as their hand.

416
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:29,999
The position of the feet...

417
00:41:30,720 --> 00:41:33,639
...will tell you where
his next move will be.

418
00:41:33,640 --> 00:41:36,799
How will you protect yourself
from the invisible enemy?

419
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:45,599
It doesn't matter my Bey.

420
00:41:45,960 --> 00:41:47,879
The heart is what matters.

421
00:41:49,200 --> 00:41:50,759
Not the eyes that see.

422
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:51,999
..or the ears.

423
00:42:04,160 --> 00:42:06,919
I know you're angry about our grandchild.

424
00:42:08,640 --> 00:42:10,599
And you train because of it.

425
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:18,759
We haven't trained in a long time.

426
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:20,439
Attack me.

427
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:39,799
Thanks for the reminder.
I told you you'd pay for it.

428
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:47,439
It's okay as long as it's you Bala.

429
00:43:10,320 --> 00:43:11,919
What's going on?

430
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:19,679
What happened to you, Begum Hatun?

431
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:28,839
Karadin, Osman Bey.

432
00:43:29,560 --> 00:43:32,239
There was a fire.

433
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:35,239
The castle was filled with it.

434
00:43:35,240 --> 00:43:36,719
What?

435
00:43:38,000 --> 00:43:39,489
How did it happen? Who did it?

436
00:43:39,489 --> 00:43:40,959
The infidels, my bey.

437
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:43,359
They hid in a secret cellar...

438
00:43:43,360 --> 00:43:45,159
...and waited for the right time.

439
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:46,759
What about...

440
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:52,679
What did I tell you Begum Hatun?

441
00:43:54,920 --> 00:43:57,279
Didn't I tell you...

442
00:43:57,280 --> 00:44:00,919
...to take your alps with
you and go to Karadin...

443
00:44:00,920 --> 00:44:04,439
...first thing in the morning
to ensure the safety there?

444
00:44:08,120 --> 00:44:09,839
What did you do?

445
00:44:09,840 --> 00:44:12,513
She wasted time at the
tents and wanted to see...

446
00:44:12,525 --> 00:44:15,039
...the punishment Hazal
Hatun was going to get.

447
00:44:17,200 --> 00:44:18,919
Then...

448
00:44:19,280 --> 00:44:22,399
...wait for your punishment.

449
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:53,959
I don't understand why you
wanted to meet here, Karesi Bey.

450
00:44:54,280 --> 00:44:56,879
In the letter you send..

451
00:44:56,880 --> 00:45:00,559
...you asked me what I
wanted as an apology...

452
00:45:01,240 --> 00:45:03,879
...because you were sorry...

453
00:45:04,640 --> 00:45:09,439
...that you let Osman
get the sacred relics.

454
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:14,839
Here.

455
00:45:17,080 --> 00:45:19,159
What I want is...

456
00:45:19,520 --> 00:45:21,039
...this!

457
00:45:33,760 --> 00:45:35,519
This is what you want?

458
00:45:35,680 --> 00:45:38,239
A bridge? Huh, Karesi Bey?

459
00:45:42,160 --> 00:45:44,559
Like you are done with
your reign in the sea...

460
00:45:44,840 --> 00:45:48,479
...and now you want the river
in my land.

461
00:45:52,120 --> 00:45:56,959
Your ships can move in these waters.

462
00:45:58,720 --> 00:46:01,479
I meant compensation, not this.

463
00:46:02,120 --> 00:46:04,879
I won't give you a single piece of land!

464
00:46:06,960 --> 00:46:09,119
You can keep your lands.

465
00:46:09,480 --> 00:46:10,919
Just give me...

466
00:46:11,760 --> 00:46:15,279
...the right to passage on...

467
00:46:15,280 --> 00:46:19,719
...this bridge that connects these lands.

468
00:46:20,800 --> 00:46:22,959
I am the one who rules over...

469
00:46:23,160 --> 00:46:26,239
...the seas among the Beys.

470
00:46:28,040 --> 00:46:32,159
But Osman is the one that controls...

471
00:46:32,560 --> 00:46:34,359
...the land trade.

472
00:46:36,600 --> 00:46:39,759
...the merchants are...

473
00:46:40,240 --> 00:46:43,039
...given passage from here...

474
00:46:43,040 --> 00:46:45,399
...the distance would be halved...

475
00:46:45,480 --> 00:46:49,719
...and the merchants that use
Osman's roads will use yours instead.

476
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:54,199
That way...

477
00:46:54,760 --> 00:46:57,359
...while my treasure is filled..

478
00:46:58,080 --> 00:47:01,519
...Osman's treasure will be empty.

479
00:47:05,520 --> 00:47:06,359
And...

480
00:47:07,680 --> 00:47:11,399
...that way, we will be able
to defeat Osman easier.

481
00:47:12,400 --> 00:47:16,519
It's a long term, but a smart plan.

482
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:19,919
We have a deal, Karesi Bey.

483
00:47:21,760 --> 00:47:23,199
But...

484
00:47:24,200 --> 00:47:27,399
...after we end Osman...

485
00:47:27,800 --> 00:47:29,239
...we will be...

486
00:47:30,400 --> 00:47:32,279
...enemies again.

487
00:47:36,040 --> 00:47:38,559
Rest assured.

488
00:47:43,200 --> 00:47:48,839
Tomorrow, a trusted friend of mine
will bring the construction materials.

489
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:53,199
He will be responsible for the
security here. His name is Arcadeus.

490
00:47:53,480 --> 00:47:56,449
He will get married in a
secret ceremony tomorrow.

491
00:47:57,000 --> 00:48:02,439
In honor of our deal, I would like to
see you in that ceremony, Karesi Bey.

492
00:48:05,960 --> 00:48:07,119
We...

493
00:48:08,480 --> 00:48:10,319
...trusted you and...

494
00:48:11,240 --> 00:48:16,319
...gave you the castle's
ownership after conquering it!

495
00:48:16,600 --> 00:48:19,319
-Forgive me Osman Bey.
-No!

496
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:23,119
I won't.

497
00:48:27,200 --> 00:48:30,399
The infidels destroyed the castle.

498
00:48:32,240 --> 00:48:34,359
They are enemies.

499
00:48:34,360 --> 00:48:36,959
Their goal is to attack.

500
00:48:37,160 --> 00:48:40,679
Your duty is to defend.

501
00:48:43,440 --> 00:48:46,479
Taking the ownership
of Karadin from you...

502
00:48:49,400 --> 00:48:51,599
...would be a reward for you.

503
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:56,159
You will keep Karadin.

504
00:49:06,160 --> 00:49:07,879
Your punishment will...

505
00:49:08,480 --> 00:49:11,039
...be this, Begum Hatun.

506
00:49:13,960 --> 00:49:15,639
With your mistake...

507
00:49:16,560 --> 00:49:19,679
...the walls have been destroyed.

508
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:22,679
You will rebuild those walls yourself!

509
00:49:26,520 --> 00:49:28,239
For one year...

510
00:49:28,880 --> 00:49:33,159
...you won't take a
share from the taxes...

511
00:49:33,360 --> 00:49:35,999
...collected around Karadin castle.

512
00:49:38,120 --> 00:49:41,479
And your share will be...

513
00:49:43,240 --> 00:49:45,319
...used to rebuild Karadin!

514
00:49:50,480 --> 00:49:51,839
And...

515
00:49:53,120 --> 00:49:55,039
...Karadin's rule...

516
00:49:56,640 --> 00:49:57,939
...from now on...

517
00:49:58,240 --> 00:50:03,999
...will be investigated by Bayhan Bey
and Gencer Bey, who are experienced Beys.

518
00:50:06,600 --> 00:50:07,879
As you wish Osman Bey.

519
00:50:23,760 --> 00:50:26,759
Kayi Tribe

520
00:50:41,520 --> 00:50:42,359
Sister.

521
00:50:44,880 --> 00:50:46,159
Sister what is it?

522
00:50:46,200 --> 00:50:47,599
Osman Bey.

523
00:50:49,120 --> 00:50:53,919
He embarrassed me in
front of Beys and Hatuns.

524
00:50:55,840 --> 00:50:59,079
Bayhan and Gencer will watch the castle.

525
00:50:59,080 --> 00:51:01,079
They'll investigate us.

526
00:51:03,760 --> 00:51:08,359
From now on we won't make a mistake Yusuf.

527
00:51:09,960 --> 00:51:13,679
Each mistake will improve Bayhan's claim.

528
00:51:17,280 --> 00:51:19,759
-And now, Hazal Ha...
-Don't.

529
00:51:20,320 --> 00:51:21,229
Don't.

530
00:51:22,600 --> 00:51:24,099
What do you mean sister?

531
00:51:24,560 --> 00:51:26,679
We know she's innocent. We must say it.

532
00:51:26,680 --> 00:51:28,679
I told them it's Hazal, Yusuf.

533
00:51:30,840 --> 00:51:33,439
Osman Bey won't trust us...

534
00:51:33,600 --> 00:51:35,239
...if I say this.

535
00:51:36,880 --> 00:51:38,559
They'll blame it on us.

536
00:51:39,480 --> 00:51:42,839
And Bayhan and Hazal will rule the castle.

537
00:51:43,400 --> 00:51:45,359
We'll even lose the castle.

538
00:51:46,720 --> 00:51:50,079
Sister if we don't
say it they'll kill her.

539
00:51:50,080 --> 00:51:52,699
You know that they'll
kill Hazal Hatun right?

540
00:51:55,560 --> 00:51:56,539
No.

541
00:51:56,760 --> 00:51:58,599
No I won't do this.

542
00:52:00,440 --> 00:52:04,039
Our honor will be ruined, Yusuf.

543
00:52:04,040 --> 00:52:05,409
What are you doing?

544
00:52:15,800 --> 00:52:16,879
Bala.

545
00:52:18,120 --> 00:52:19,509
Don't look like that.

546
00:52:19,960 --> 00:52:21,499
I know you want to say

547
00:52:21,880 --> 00:52:23,279
...'I told you so.'

548
00:52:23,600 --> 00:52:25,119
I indeed do.

549
00:52:28,280 --> 00:52:30,239
But despite my opinion...

550
00:52:30,920 --> 00:52:32,639
...you gave the castle to her.

551
00:52:37,920 --> 00:52:38,799
Yes I did.

552
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:40,999
You did...

553
00:52:42,040 --> 00:52:44,759
....but Hatun made a mistake.

554
00:52:45,240 --> 00:52:47,639
Is this the punishment for it, Osman Bey?

555
00:52:48,400 --> 00:52:51,959
Why didn't you take the
castle despite such a mistake

556
00:52:52,280 --> 00:52:53,519
No.

557
00:52:55,120 --> 00:52:56,719
A single mistake...

558
00:52:57,280 --> 00:52:58,719
...won't result in that.

559
00:53:00,520 --> 00:53:02,519
And we talked about it Bala.

560
00:53:02,920 --> 00:53:06,839
Begum Hatun doesn't feel close to us.

561
00:53:07,240 --> 00:53:08,199
No.

562
00:53:08,880 --> 00:53:10,519
It doesn't seem so.

563
00:53:12,880 --> 00:53:14,119
Maybe you don't see it.

564
00:53:15,560 --> 00:53:16,799
See what?

565
00:53:21,280 --> 00:53:25,079
Begum Hatun has a close bond with Kayi.

566
00:53:30,880 --> 00:53:32,489
What are you saying Bala?

567
00:53:34,360 --> 00:53:35,679
Do you think so?

568
00:53:37,520 --> 00:53:38,279
She does.

569
00:53:41,280 --> 00:53:43,599
And this bond is so tight...

570
00:53:43,920 --> 00:53:46,079
...that she gets smothered.

571
00:53:47,680 --> 00:53:49,639
That's why she makes mistakes.

572
00:53:52,360 --> 00:53:54,149
Such kind of bond, you know?

573
00:54:10,960 --> 00:54:12,039
Baysungur.

574
00:54:20,200 --> 00:54:23,759
My Bey. I followed
Karesi Bey as you wished.

575
00:54:23,920 --> 00:54:25,279
I watched his every move.

576
00:54:26,320 --> 00:54:27,759
I have important news.

577
00:54:28,120 --> 00:54:28,959
Tell me.

578
00:54:45,200 --> 00:54:47,279
What's in that cart?

579
00:54:50,080 --> 00:54:52,679
I hope it's not someone from our side.

580
00:55:01,120 --> 00:55:02,879
May Allah protect us.

581
00:55:06,880 --> 00:55:08,559
What is he doing here?

582
00:55:08,560 --> 00:55:11,119
Take your soldiers and leave.

583
00:55:19,920 --> 00:55:21,319
My bey.

584
00:55:21,320 --> 00:55:23,079
Byzantine commander Lucas is here.

585
00:55:23,080 --> 00:55:26,359
He has a cart with him.
He wants to see you.

586
00:55:29,680 --> 00:55:30,839
Let him.

587
00:55:36,520 --> 00:55:38,679
Give us your swords.

588
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:02,239
Yusuf, stop. Where are you going?

589
00:56:03,040 --> 00:56:05,839
I'm going to tell Osman Bey the truth.

590
00:56:05,840 --> 00:56:11,039
Sister, even if you can feel at ease
with this secret I can't feel at ease.

591
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:27,839
Yusuf don't do this
brother, we'll get in trouble.

592
00:56:59,720 --> 00:57:02,359
What is it commander Lucas?

593
00:57:03,120 --> 00:57:05,799
What is this thing that
you say is very important?

594
00:57:07,200 --> 00:57:09,999
Who is under that cloth?

595
00:57:14,400 --> 00:57:19,759
You can't thank me enough Osman Bey.

596
00:57:48,480 --> 00:57:51,719
This traitor whom I've killed myself...

597
00:57:52,240 --> 00:57:55,519
...is the one who caused
your grandkid's death.

598
00:57:57,440 --> 00:57:58,839
Gonca.

599
00:58:03,600 --> 00:58:05,279
Is she the one?

600
00:58:05,280 --> 00:58:07,399
Did she kill my baby?

601
00:58:07,400 --> 00:58:09,159
Alaeddin.

602
00:58:09,160 --> 00:58:10,119
Mother.

603
00:58:10,120 --> 00:58:10,919
-Girl.
-Okay.

604
00:58:10,920 --> 00:58:13,799
-Okay Gonca.
-Okay girl wait.

605
00:58:19,400 --> 00:58:20,999
-Okay Gonca.
-I know her.

606
00:58:21,000 --> 00:58:23,439
She was with Holofira. I've seen her.

607
00:58:23,440 --> 00:58:25,039
-I have, Alaeddin.
-Okay Gonca.

608
00:58:25,040 --> 00:58:27,799
She was with Holofira. I've seen her.

609
00:58:27,800 --> 00:58:29,639
They killed my baby.

610
00:58:29,640 --> 00:58:31,959
Holofira is innocent.

611
00:58:36,040 --> 00:58:38,319
Cecillia's father..

612
00:58:38,480 --> 00:58:40,999
...died while fighting you Turks.

613
00:58:41,000 --> 00:58:46,879
That vicious Magnus used her hatred and
made her snuggle poison into your tribe.

614
00:58:51,320 --> 00:58:53,479
Commander Lucas.

615
00:58:54,560 --> 00:58:56,999
Come into the tent...

616
00:58:57,000 --> 00:59:00,359
...and let's talk about this in depth.

617
00:59:13,680 --> 00:59:14,559
Baykurt.

618
00:59:14,560 --> 00:59:15,719
My bey.

619
00:59:15,720 --> 00:59:17,639
Tell The Sisters..

620
00:59:17,640 --> 00:59:19,959
...to let Hazal Hatun go.

621
00:59:19,960 --> 00:59:21,799
As you wish my bey.

622
00:59:32,480 --> 00:59:35,759
The arm of the Turks cannot be bent...

623
00:59:36,840 --> 00:59:40,559
The power of the Turks never runs out.

624
00:59:45,600 --> 00:59:47,839
Now that's it.

625
00:59:49,760 --> 00:59:53,479
I am still young. I shouldn't
have any white hair!

626
00:59:59,840 --> 01:00:03,039
I paid 5 pouches of coin for it...

627
01:00:03,960 --> 01:00:06,519
...but it's good that I bought it early.

628
01:00:07,680 --> 01:00:09,759
I made a profit.

629
01:00:12,080 --> 01:00:14,719
Hazal Hatun's future is unknown.

630
01:00:14,720 --> 01:00:17,039
I may need new jewelry.

631
01:00:30,480 --> 01:00:32,399
You look good, father.

632
01:00:34,440 --> 01:00:36,359
Your hatun is waiting for her death...

633
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:38,999
...and you are preparing for a wedding.

634
01:00:39,360 --> 01:00:42,079
Stop talking nonsense.

635
01:00:44,000 --> 01:00:46,319
When your mother comes back to me...

636
01:00:46,560 --> 01:00:49,919
...I should look good for her.

637
01:00:49,920 --> 01:00:50,879
Father.

638
01:00:52,160 --> 01:00:54,359
If you think about my mother...

639
01:00:54,520 --> 01:00:56,639
...then why did you stop us from escaping?

640
01:00:58,720 --> 01:01:01,079
Either you have a different plan...

641
01:01:03,920 --> 01:01:05,199
...or a different hatun on your mind.

642
01:01:05,200 --> 01:01:06,839
What plan?

643
01:01:08,400 --> 01:01:12,079
We couldn't challenge Osman Bey's justice.

644
01:01:12,680 --> 01:01:14,639
I am back!

645
01:01:16,000 --> 01:01:17,799
I am back for real!

646
01:01:17,800 --> 01:01:19,239
Mother!

647
01:01:19,400 --> 01:01:22,279
I am saved! I am free!

648
01:01:22,400 --> 01:01:24,159
Mother, how did that happen?

649
01:01:24,160 --> 01:01:25,599
My son.

650
01:01:26,080 --> 01:01:28,999
I will tell you all.

651
01:01:29,000 --> 01:01:30,399
My dear mother.

652
01:01:37,680 --> 01:01:39,839
What's this?

653
01:01:44,160 --> 01:01:45,559
What's this?

654
01:01:46,320 --> 01:01:50,559
I was in the dungeon and
you were shaping your beard?

655
01:01:57,440 --> 01:01:59,719
It looks good.

656
01:02:01,640 --> 01:02:03,279
It looks good, but...

657
01:02:03,520 --> 01:02:06,599
...instead of trying to save me...

658
01:02:06,640 --> 01:02:09,199
...were you thinking
of getting a new hatun?

659
01:02:09,200 --> 01:02:11,559
Is that why you did this?

660
01:02:12,480 --> 01:02:15,279
Of course not, my hatun.

661
01:02:15,760 --> 01:02:18,039
I did it for you.

662
01:02:18,160 --> 01:02:21,279
I knew that the truth would be revealed.

663
01:02:21,520 --> 01:02:25,359
Mother, look what my
father bought for you.

664
01:02:37,840 --> 01:02:41,519
He paid 5 pouches of gold for it.

665
01:02:46,800 --> 01:02:48,839
My Bey, really?

666
01:02:48,840 --> 01:02:50,999
For real, mother.

667
01:02:51,280 --> 01:02:53,079
He said you deserve the whole world.

668
01:02:53,360 --> 01:02:55,989
He said anything would be good on you.

669
01:02:57,040 --> 01:03:00,359
My Bayhan. My brave Bey.

670
01:03:01,280 --> 01:03:04,199
You knew it, huh?

671
01:03:06,600 --> 01:03:09,479
I knew it, my hatun.

672
01:03:10,600 --> 01:03:12,439
Go on, put it on me.

673
01:03:12,440 --> 01:03:15,319
You chose nicely, father.

674
01:03:15,320 --> 01:03:17,319
It's beautiful.

675
01:03:17,680 --> 01:03:19,679
Father, go on.

676
01:03:21,280 --> 01:03:22,639
It's beautiful.

677
01:03:23,280 --> 01:03:25,599
Bayhan, aren't you doing it too tight?

678
01:03:25,600 --> 01:03:27,199
Father.

679
01:03:27,800 --> 01:03:29,039
Father.

680
01:03:32,280 --> 01:03:33,959
It looks good.

681
01:03:40,000 --> 01:03:43,199
The stealing of sacred relics.

682
01:03:44,920 --> 01:03:46,919
That ignoble dog Cecilia's coming...

683
01:03:47,280 --> 01:03:50,639
...to our table!

684
01:03:50,800 --> 01:03:55,199
What happened in Karadin Castle...

685
01:03:55,800 --> 01:03:58,239
...which is under Begum Hatun's rule.

686
01:03:58,920 --> 01:04:00,799
All of that...

687
01:04:01,920 --> 01:04:03,719
...was planned...

688
01:04:04,360 --> 01:04:06,359
...by Magnus, huh?

689
01:04:08,320 --> 01:04:09,839
Yes.

690
01:04:11,680 --> 01:04:13,919
That dastard called Magnus...

691
01:04:13,920 --> 01:04:16,519
...was part of an organization...

692
01:04:16,720 --> 01:04:20,599
...that sneaked into the
deepest parts of the empire.

693
01:04:22,520 --> 01:04:25,359
Traitors are everywhere, Osman Bey.

694
01:04:30,160 --> 01:04:33,559
If you had not...

695
01:04:33,760 --> 01:04:37,239
...brought that girl to me dead...

696
01:04:37,400 --> 01:04:40,799
...and gave her to
me to interrogate her...

697
01:04:41,760 --> 01:04:43,919
...then I would have believed you!

698
01:04:45,800 --> 01:04:47,279
Unfortunately.

699
01:04:48,280 --> 01:04:51,479
She threatened to kill me
when I accused him of treason.

700
01:04:52,200 --> 01:04:54,679
So I had to kill her.

701
01:04:56,560 --> 01:04:58,399
I assure you...

702
01:04:59,240 --> 01:05:01,239
...I don't get involved in games.

703
01:05:03,160 --> 01:05:06,719
I look my enemy in the eyes.

704
01:05:07,240 --> 01:05:09,159
And stab them in the heart.

705
01:05:11,560 --> 01:05:12,399
Fearlessly.

706
01:05:13,240 --> 01:05:14,399
Like you.

707
01:05:15,560 --> 01:05:17,799
If the traitor Magnus...

708
01:05:18,000 --> 01:05:22,639
If you hadn't killed him I'd
burn him in the middle of Bursa.

709
01:05:23,680 --> 01:05:26,799
Now, despite what I told you...

710
01:05:28,440 --> 01:05:30,759
...if you still blame me for this...

711
01:05:31,840 --> 01:05:33,599
...it's your choice.

712
01:05:34,120 --> 01:05:34,999
I respect it.

713
01:05:36,800 --> 01:05:37,959
Excuse me.

714
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:39,879
Wait.

715
01:05:41,080 --> 01:05:42,359
Wait.

716
01:05:47,080 --> 01:05:48,749
Whether a man is...

717
01:05:51,200 --> 01:05:52,399
...fearful...

718
01:05:53,160 --> 01:05:54,679
...or brave...

719
01:05:55,880 --> 01:05:57,529
...depends on action...

720
01:05:58,320 --> 01:06:00,119
..not words.

721
01:06:01,320 --> 01:06:02,799
We'll see.

722
01:06:02,960 --> 01:06:06,159
We'll see if what you say is true...

723
01:06:08,240 --> 01:06:10,119
...or not.

724
01:06:22,600 --> 01:06:23,719
I trusted her the most.

725
01:06:23,760 --> 01:06:24,679
Gonca.

726
01:06:25,120 --> 01:06:27,239
How could you do this Holofira?

727
01:06:27,240 --> 01:06:28,839
How could you?

728
01:06:28,840 --> 01:06:30,159
I trusted her the most.

729
01:06:30,160 --> 01:06:32,079
Okay Gonca hold on.

730
01:06:32,080 --> 01:06:34,679
I called her my sister Alaeddin.

731
01:06:34,680 --> 01:06:36,239
Calm down sweetheart.

732
01:06:36,400 --> 01:06:40,239
She's the reason our baby died Alaeddin.

733
01:06:40,240 --> 01:06:42,239
Gonca. Calm down.

734
01:06:43,200 --> 01:06:45,319
Holofira didn't know. How could she?

735
01:06:45,320 --> 01:06:46,359
She should have.

736
01:06:46,880 --> 01:06:48,279
She should have.

737
01:06:49,120 --> 01:06:51,599
She should have.

738
01:06:56,520 --> 01:06:58,479
Our baby died.

739
01:06:58,480 --> 01:07:02,199
I sat down next to my baby's killer.

740
01:07:02,320 --> 01:07:04,239
I ate the same food with them!

741
01:07:04,240 --> 01:07:06,239
Look. It's gone.

742
01:07:06,320 --> 01:07:08,559
My baby's gone Alaeddin.

743
01:07:08,760 --> 01:07:09,489
It's gone.

744
01:07:09,489 --> 01:07:11,279
Gonca

745
01:07:12,200 --> 01:07:13,239
Hold on.

746
01:07:13,560 --> 01:07:15,759
You loved her she loved you.

747
01:07:15,760 --> 01:07:16,999
You were sisters.

748
01:07:17,000 --> 01:07:18,119
It's over.

749
01:07:18,760 --> 01:07:21,399
It's over. It's over Alaeddin.

750
01:07:22,680 --> 01:07:24,999
We're not friends.

751
01:07:25,400 --> 01:07:28,079
She's the reason my baby died.

752
01:07:30,760 --> 01:07:33,439
She's the reason my baby died Alaeddin.

753
01:07:37,640 --> 01:07:38,399
It's over.

754
01:07:40,400 --> 01:07:43,079
To stop our trade business here...

755
01:07:44,280 --> 01:07:47,839
...and to weaken our state...

756
01:07:48,360 --> 01:07:50,079
...he's working with Lucas.

757
01:07:51,080 --> 01:07:52,039
True, my Bey.

758
01:07:58,000 --> 01:07:59,479
Karesi Bey.

759
01:08:00,960 --> 01:08:04,839
I guess you went behind our backs.

760
01:08:08,080 --> 01:08:09,639
This is the second mistake.

761
01:08:10,640 --> 01:08:14,079
I guess he's annoyed
about the relics issue.

762
01:08:14,440 --> 01:08:17,078
He's furious my Bey.

763
01:08:17,560 --> 01:08:19,439
He hits our trade today...

764
01:08:19,720 --> 01:08:21,999
...tomorrow it's something else.

765
01:08:22,160 --> 01:08:23,999
Karesi won't sit quietly.

766
01:08:31,120 --> 01:08:32,999
What do you think?

767
01:08:33,000 --> 01:08:34,999
I think this is tomorrow's business.

768
01:08:35,399 --> 01:08:38,519
What will we do about the bridge?

769
01:08:38,800 --> 01:08:40,769
We must talk about it first.

770
01:08:41,720 --> 01:08:45,559
No trade means no money, Osman Bey.

771
01:08:46,080 --> 01:08:50,158
Allah forbid, if Lucas
finishes the bridge...

772
01:08:50,960 --> 01:08:53,559
...and Karesi Bey
gets what he wants...

773
01:08:54,560 --> 01:08:56,599
...we can't get strong again.

774
01:08:57,200 --> 01:08:58,999
They won't finish the bridge.

775
01:09:00,319 --> 01:09:01,759
And we will never fail.

776
01:09:06,840 --> 01:09:07,759
Tomorrow...

777
01:09:08,319 --> 01:09:11,037
...the other supplies for the bridge...

778
01:09:11,240 --> 01:09:13,809
...and Lucas will be
there, right Baysungur?

779
01:09:13,960 --> 01:09:15,238
True my Bey.

780
01:09:16,279 --> 01:09:17,919
Alright.

781
01:09:19,359 --> 01:09:21,639
Gencer Bey, Bayhan Bey.

782
01:09:21,880 --> 01:09:23,078
Finish preparation.

783
01:09:23,640 --> 01:09:25,158
We'll head out tonight.

784
01:09:31,840 --> 01:09:32,759
Orhan.

785
01:09:33,040 --> 01:09:34,119
My Bey.

786
01:09:34,560 --> 01:09:36,049
You're in charge of the tribe.

787
01:09:36,120 --> 01:09:37,548
As you wish my Bey.

788
01:09:38,240 --> 01:09:41,279
When we rain on them like wildfire...

789
01:09:42,520 --> 01:09:44,319
...they will see...

790
01:09:44,920 --> 01:09:46,359
...what an alliance is.

791
01:10:21,480 --> 01:10:24,159
This necklace will suit...

792
01:10:25,480 --> 01:10:28,399
...that elegant neck of yours...

793
01:10:28,520 --> 01:10:30,319
... Begum Hatun.

794
01:10:35,880 --> 01:10:37,439
My bey.

795
01:10:37,600 --> 01:10:41,570
Osman Bey is going to punish
Begum Hatun because of her...

796
01:10:41,570 --> 01:10:43,719
..reckless behavior at Karadin Castle.

797
01:10:43,720 --> 01:10:45,399
Certainly.

798
01:10:47,280 --> 01:10:52,039
That's why we're making
our move right now.

799
01:10:55,000 --> 01:10:57,599
Send out a messenger.

800
01:11:00,120 --> 01:11:04,199
Give this letter and the necklace...

801
01:11:09,520 --> 01:11:14,039
...to Begum Hatun secretly.

802
01:11:15,400 --> 01:11:17,439
Secretly.

803
01:11:18,400 --> 01:11:20,319
As you wish my bey.

804
01:11:31,080 --> 01:11:34,079
My bey the tradesmen you called came.

805
01:11:34,240 --> 01:11:36,399
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be with you.

806
01:11:36,720 --> 01:11:38,719
Peace be upon you.

807
01:11:39,200 --> 01:11:42,199
Now the era of...

808
01:11:42,560 --> 01:11:45,559
...traveling for a long time is over.

809
01:11:47,040 --> 01:11:50,639
The road that takes
you 40 days to cross...

810
01:11:50,640 --> 01:11:55,199
...and for which you have
to pay taxes will be down to half.

811
01:11:57,600 --> 01:12:00,439
Now, tell me.

812
01:12:01,120 --> 01:12:04,359
Will you use my roads for your caravans?

813
01:12:04,360 --> 01:12:06,679
We will Karesi Bey.

814
01:12:08,800 --> 01:12:09,759
Thank you.

815
01:12:26,120 --> 01:12:28,239
What will we do with this Gencer Bey?

816
01:12:28,240 --> 01:12:30,879
What does Osman Bey have in mind?

817
01:12:30,880 --> 01:12:34,799
Osman Bey never lets on his secrets.

818
01:12:37,080 --> 01:12:41,719
Osman Bey only talks about his
moves while he is executing them, beys.

819
01:12:51,840 --> 01:12:57,279
The one who thought of climbing those
walls can do anything with these logs.

820
01:12:59,280 --> 01:13:01,039
Come on.

821
01:13:04,520 --> 01:13:06,839
Are the preparations done?

822
01:13:06,840 --> 01:13:08,839
Everything's ready my bey.

823
01:13:08,840 --> 01:13:11,199
What will we do now?

824
01:13:13,960 --> 01:13:17,319
We'll attack the inn
of the jackal like a wolf.

825
01:13:22,000 --> 01:13:23,599
Good.

826
01:13:24,320 --> 01:13:25,639
Good.

827
01:13:31,800 --> 01:13:35,999
Mother, brother. This
note was on Cecillia.

828
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:38,119
It's from Holofira.

829
01:13:38,840 --> 01:13:40,919
What's going oh girl?

830
01:13:48,000 --> 01:13:49,359
Orhan.

831
01:13:57,560 --> 01:13:59,719
That damn Lucas.

832
01:14:00,040 --> 01:14:02,919
He's making Holofira
marry against her will.

833
01:14:03,080 --> 01:14:06,119
Where? When? Do we know?

834
01:14:06,680 --> 01:14:08,239
Tomorrow.

835
01:14:09,040 --> 01:14:12,279
It will happen at the skirts of
the Monk Mountain. Mother.

836
01:14:12,680 --> 01:14:13,999
Don't.

837
01:14:14,000 --> 01:14:16,639
Don't tell me to stop.

838
01:14:23,760 --> 01:14:26,079
I'll take care of the tribe son.

839
01:14:27,360 --> 01:14:30,679
Go and kidnap my daughter in law.

840
01:14:30,800 --> 01:14:31,879
It's time.

841
01:14:31,880 --> 01:14:33,399
I will.

842
01:14:37,320 --> 01:14:38,999
I will.

843
01:14:42,320 --> 01:14:45,479
How many times have you
kidnapped Holofira, brother?

844
01:14:45,680 --> 01:14:48,839
I stopped counting.

845
01:14:54,840 --> 01:14:58,119
Just as how we kidnapped Gonca...

846
01:14:58,880 --> 01:15:01,759
...we will get Holofira the same way.

847
01:15:03,600 --> 01:15:04,999
Right Gonca?

848
01:15:06,240 --> 01:15:08,759
Excuse me in this matter, mother.

849
01:15:10,080 --> 01:15:11,719
I can't come with you.

850
01:15:19,000 --> 01:15:21,039
You may go to that wedding...

851
01:15:21,800 --> 01:15:23,799
...but it's dangerous, Orhan Bey.

852
01:15:25,440 --> 01:15:27,949
It looks like you are
going to center of the danger.

853
01:15:28,720 --> 01:15:30,479
May Allah help you.

854
01:15:31,280 --> 01:15:32,599
Gonca.

855
01:15:36,560 --> 01:15:38,239
Don't be like this, sister.

856
01:15:40,400 --> 01:15:43,159
You love Holofira like your sister.

857
01:15:46,680 --> 01:15:48,199
That's why...

858
01:15:50,520 --> 01:15:52,799
...I feel hurt.

859
01:15:56,320 --> 01:15:58,079
I lost my baby...

860
01:16:00,200 --> 01:16:02,599
...and my sister.

861
01:17:16,520 --> 01:17:19,319
Son, Gonca was right.

862
01:17:19,800 --> 01:17:21,279
It will be dangerous.

863
01:17:21,280 --> 01:17:22,959
I don't care what happens, mother.

864
01:17:23,440 --> 01:17:25,759
I won't leave Holofira alone.

865
01:17:26,600 --> 01:17:29,479
I am not telling you to stop.

866
01:17:29,760 --> 01:17:32,399
Just be cautious.

867
01:17:34,680 --> 01:17:36,799
Take your most skilled alps.

868
01:17:36,800 --> 01:17:39,279
Orhan..

869
01:17:39,800 --> 01:17:42,269
...I should come with
you together with The Sisters.

870
01:17:42,269 --> 01:17:43,509
No, mother.

871
01:17:44,120 --> 01:17:46,039
My father is not here either.

872
01:17:46,040 --> 01:17:49,319
If you come with me, there
won't be anyone left in the tribe.

873
01:17:49,960 --> 01:17:54,119
And as for the alps, the
fewer we are, the better.

874
01:17:56,800 --> 01:17:59,879
Okay.

875
01:18:00,080 --> 01:18:03,359
Lucas keeps this wedding a secret.

876
01:18:03,720 --> 01:18:05,959
He must have taken precautions.

877
01:18:06,280 --> 01:18:08,839
I am sending you to a
fire with my own hands.

878
01:18:09,960 --> 01:18:11,559
Mother.

879
01:18:13,840 --> 01:18:15,439
Pray.

880
01:18:15,960 --> 01:18:17,679
Pray.

881
01:18:18,040 --> 01:18:21,719
I will bring your
daughter-in-law safe and sound.

882
01:18:22,600 --> 01:18:25,519
If Allah permits, my son.

883
01:18:26,240 --> 01:18:29,839
Look, take the best alps.

884
01:18:32,200 --> 01:18:35,079
Turahan, you choose the alps.

885
01:18:35,840 --> 01:18:38,079
But tell them this is
not a matter of state...

886
01:18:38,080 --> 01:18:41,839
...but my personal matter.
Only the volunteers should come.

887
01:18:42,680 --> 01:18:45,199
We will hit the road at dawn.

888
01:18:45,440 --> 01:18:47,599
As you command, my shahzade.

889
01:18:48,920 --> 01:18:50,839
Now it's your turn, Baysungur.

890
01:18:51,360 --> 01:18:55,319
That dastard called Lucas must
have kept all the roads going there.

891
01:18:55,840 --> 01:18:57,119
Now tell me.

892
01:18:57,680 --> 01:19:00,879
How are we going to enter the wedding?

893
01:19:01,480 --> 01:19:04,679
Now, my shahzade, our path is tough...

894
01:19:07,120 --> 01:19:09,079
..but this is...

895
01:19:10,720 --> 01:19:12,279
...the shortest way.

896
01:19:16,120 --> 01:19:19,159
My mother is right, brother.

897
01:19:19,400 --> 01:19:21,479
Let's say you kidnapped Holofira.

898
01:19:21,480 --> 01:19:23,919
How are you going to get out of that hell?

899
01:19:25,520 --> 01:19:27,039
When I...

900
01:19:28,080 --> 01:19:31,679
...get Holofira from there safely...

901
01:19:32,680 --> 01:19:34,519
...the rest is easy.

902
01:19:46,600 --> 01:19:49,719
Commander Lucas sent your
wedding dress Princess Holofira.

903
01:20:00,720 --> 01:20:04,039
-If you wish, you can deco...
-No.

904
01:20:05,080 --> 01:20:07,079
Get out. I want to be alone.

905
01:20:47,880 --> 01:20:49,439
Orhan.

906
01:20:53,640 --> 01:20:57,319
I can't live anywhere
other than by your side.

907
01:20:58,880 --> 01:20:59,679
I know it.

908
01:21:02,360 --> 01:21:04,559
If you got the letter...

909
01:21:05,120 --> 01:21:06,959
...you'll come to save me.

910
01:21:10,960 --> 01:21:12,879
But if you can't...

911
01:21:14,960 --> 01:21:16,959
...I won't live in this hell.

912
01:21:28,960 --> 01:21:30,399
I'll kill him.

913
01:21:33,360 --> 01:21:35,599
Even if I die at the end.

914
01:21:37,920 --> 01:21:39,919
I won't marry anyone other than you.

915
01:23:25,360 --> 01:23:30,839
Across the river, we'll do the
same to all watchers of the bridge.

916
01:23:31,120 --> 01:23:32,559
Dastards.

917
01:23:32,720 --> 01:23:34,959
The order they set up
thanks to their treason...

918
01:23:34,959 --> 01:23:37,289
...will befall to their heads
like that bridge, my Bey.

919
01:23:37,289 --> 01:23:38,399
True, true.

920
01:23:38,400 --> 01:23:42,859
But Turk's future will be written
by men who fight the infidels...

921
01:23:43,520 --> 01:23:45,679
...not those who work with them.

922
01:23:45,800 --> 01:23:46,719
Come on.

923
01:23:58,880 --> 01:24:01,919
No gem can be worthy of you.

924
01:24:02,960 --> 01:24:05,999
But this pearl necklace out of the sea...

925
01:24:06,080 --> 01:24:09,199
...is a sign of our friendship.

926
01:24:34,480 --> 01:24:38,279
Tomorrow I'd like to invite you
to talk about a serious matter.

927
01:24:38,600 --> 01:24:41,319
I'd appreciate it if you accept my offer.

928
01:24:41,720 --> 01:24:43,759
I assure you of that.

929
01:24:44,160 --> 01:24:45,839
Karesi Bey.

930
01:25:13,920 --> 01:25:16,439
This was the last on my bey.

931
01:25:16,720 --> 01:25:19,799
Let's go and destroy the bridge.

932
01:25:20,040 --> 01:25:24,239
Let's fall down on them
like this dark night, my bey.

933
01:25:24,360 --> 01:25:25,839
No.

934
01:25:26,520 --> 01:25:27,919
We're going to wait.

935
01:25:27,920 --> 01:25:31,079
They don't have anyone
left to go help them, my bey.

936
01:25:31,080 --> 01:25:33,559
It's just the time to attack them my bey.

937
01:25:33,560 --> 01:25:35,239
It is.

938
01:25:35,240 --> 01:25:40,279
But Lucas will send the
rest of the stuff for the bridge.

939
01:25:40,640 --> 01:25:45,479
When he brings them here,
we'll destroy them with the bridge.

940
01:25:45,760 --> 01:25:49,599
They'll see what it means
to set fire to our lands.

941
01:25:49,840 --> 01:25:52,519
He'll pay for it all.

942
01:25:52,520 --> 01:25:53,919
All of it.

943
01:26:08,680 --> 01:26:10,599
Ayse Hatun.

944
01:26:10,600 --> 01:26:12,679
I'll leave for duty.

945
01:26:12,880 --> 01:26:16,559
Don't be naughty while I'm away.

946
01:26:17,200 --> 01:26:21,919
You are leaving and am I
staying here? I'll come with you.

947
01:26:23,440 --> 01:26:26,919
If you leave what will we have for dinner?

948
01:26:28,200 --> 01:26:32,079
I'll talk with Ulgen Hatun,
she'll cook something.

949
01:26:35,960 --> 01:26:37,239
Ayse.

950
01:26:39,560 --> 01:26:42,439
Where did you find that dagger?

951
01:26:45,480 --> 01:26:48,319
Didn't I tell you not to open that chest?

952
01:26:49,600 --> 01:26:52,799
Ghazi has all kinds of swords. I don't.

953
01:26:52,800 --> 01:26:55,719
What should I do? Be left behind?

954
01:26:55,720 --> 01:26:58,039
You always get mad at me.

955
01:27:04,800 --> 01:27:07,359
It's your grandpa's dagger right?

956
01:27:07,360 --> 01:27:09,559
That's why you don't let me touch it.

957
01:27:13,400 --> 01:27:15,119
It is.

958
01:27:16,600 --> 01:27:22,039
The son of Suleyman Shah, my
grandpa, Sungurtekin. It belongs to him.

959
01:27:31,840 --> 01:27:36,879
But only two of us will know that
we belong to the Kayi bloodline.

960
01:27:37,840 --> 01:27:40,839
I promise I'll get you
a sword once I'm back.

961
01:27:42,800 --> 01:27:46,839
But, you have to make
a promise to me now too.

962
01:27:47,520 --> 01:27:49,879
You won't open this chest again.

963
01:27:50,040 --> 01:27:51,559
I promise.

964
01:27:51,560 --> 01:27:54,639
Good job, my beautiful daughter.

965
01:27:56,480 --> 01:27:57,999
Come on.

966
01:28:10,240 --> 01:28:13,319
You make me promise so much that...

967
01:28:13,560 --> 01:28:16,559
...I forget what I promise for.

968
01:28:18,920 --> 01:28:20,799
Have an easy journey, son.

969
01:28:20,800 --> 01:28:22,519
I'll pray for you.

970
01:28:22,520 --> 01:28:24,239
Thank you mother.

971
01:28:28,400 --> 01:28:29,999
Orhan Bey.

972
01:28:30,320 --> 01:28:32,599
If you allow me, I want to come with you.

973
01:28:32,600 --> 01:28:34,719
I know how tough those roads can be.

974
01:28:34,840 --> 01:28:36,519
Thank you Ilbay.

975
01:28:36,720 --> 01:28:38,119
You can come.

976
01:28:43,240 --> 01:28:44,839
Brother.

977
01:28:46,560 --> 01:28:48,079
Brother.

978
01:28:48,080 --> 01:28:49,719
I'll come with you.

979
01:28:49,720 --> 01:28:52,639
I can't send you
alone in this situation.

980
01:28:52,640 --> 01:28:53,999
Sister.

981
01:28:54,400 --> 01:28:56,279
You stay here.

982
01:28:56,280 --> 01:28:59,199
My mother needs you.

983
01:29:11,600 --> 01:29:12,959
Besides...

984
01:29:15,240 --> 01:29:19,119
...you can't leave Gonca Hatun
alone in this situation either.

985
01:29:19,120 --> 01:29:20,599
Brother.

986
01:29:20,600 --> 01:29:22,359
You're going to fight.

987
01:29:22,440 --> 01:29:24,079
With only so few alps...

988
01:29:24,080 --> 01:29:25,639
Orhan Bey.

989
01:29:27,240 --> 01:29:30,919
I've heard that you're
going to fight for your love.

990
01:29:31,600 --> 01:29:35,239
If you allow me, I want
to join you in your fight.

991
01:29:36,160 --> 01:29:38,559
Thank you Yusuf Bey.

992
01:29:46,960 --> 01:29:48,159
Come on Alps!

993
01:30:02,480 --> 01:30:04,639
Come on Saruca, you go too!

994
01:30:04,640 --> 01:30:05,959
No, mother!

995
01:30:06,560 --> 01:30:08,999
I can't jump into the fire like that.

996
01:30:13,840 --> 01:30:16,679
What is it Saruca Bey, are you coming too?

997
01:30:18,200 --> 01:30:21,519
In a duty like this, I cannot...

998
01:30:24,880 --> 01:30:26,959
...leave you alone, Orhan Bey.

999
01:30:26,960 --> 01:30:28,319
I am with you.

1000
01:30:28,680 --> 01:30:30,639
Thank you. Come.

1001
01:30:33,320 --> 01:30:34,799
Thanks, mother.

1002
01:30:47,520 --> 01:30:50,449
In the name of Allah, the most
merciful, the most beneficent.

1003
01:30:59,880 --> 01:31:02,949
In the name of Allah, the most
merciful, the most beneficent.

1004
01:31:05,520 --> 01:31:08,039
Safe travels, son.

1005
01:31:12,840 --> 01:31:15,759
So, Bala Hatun.

1006
01:31:16,600 --> 01:31:19,519
Aren't you going to tell me
where the shahzade is going?

1007
01:31:21,680 --> 01:31:25,399
She is going to bring my
daughter-in-law back, Hazal Hatun.

1008
01:31:39,960 --> 01:31:41,119
My girl.

1009
01:31:41,840 --> 01:31:43,919
Send a messenger to your father.

1010
01:31:43,920 --> 01:31:47,119
I don't feel at ease sending Orhan alone.

1011
01:31:48,200 --> 01:31:50,279
As you command mother.

1012
01:32:53,840 --> 01:32:58,119
Arcadeus. This is the bridge
that will drain Osman's treasury.

1013
01:32:58,320 --> 01:33:01,079
I want it to be finished quickly.

1014
01:33:01,480 --> 01:33:06,199
Turkish slaves from
Bursa were born for this job.

1015
01:33:07,040 --> 01:33:10,439
They should work and die here.

1016
01:33:10,440 --> 01:33:13,559
You are right. They deserve to die.

1017
01:33:19,560 --> 01:33:23,839
Thanks to this bridge,
Turks will fight each other.

1018
01:33:23,960 --> 01:33:28,079
Karesi will win, and
Osman will attack him.

1019
01:33:36,800 --> 01:33:39,799
Oh Allah!

1020
01:34:31,120 --> 01:34:32,639
Allah. Come on!

1021
01:34:38,600 --> 01:34:39,919
Damn it!

1022
01:34:51,560 --> 01:34:53,199
Osman!

1023
01:35:00,360 --> 01:35:01,879
Osman!

1024
01:35:05,120 --> 01:35:05,959
Lucas!

1025
01:35:15,080 --> 01:35:16,999
I brought you hell!

1026
01:35:20,680 --> 01:35:23,359
Send help from the watcher posts!

1027
01:35:24,320 --> 01:35:26,399
Alps! Attack!

1028
01:35:26,400 --> 01:35:29,119
Allah is the Greatest!

1029
01:35:46,040 --> 01:35:47,759
You're generous, Karesi Bey.

1030
01:35:49,920 --> 01:35:51,279
Thank you.

1031
01:35:51,880 --> 01:35:54,199
But I can't accept it.

1032
01:35:58,880 --> 01:36:01,559
What did I tell you...

1033
01:36:04,080 --> 01:36:05,559
...when we first met?

1034
01:36:07,720 --> 01:36:09,429
You are higher than a Bey.

1035
01:36:09,760 --> 01:36:11,479
You're higher than a Khan.

1036
01:36:12,120 --> 01:36:15,439
And you deserve the best gems.

1037
01:36:15,960 --> 01:36:17,599
Begum Hatun.

1038
01:36:22,880 --> 01:36:24,279
Don't wear it for now.

1039
01:36:27,840 --> 01:36:29,039
But...

1040
01:36:30,600 --> 01:36:32,039
...keep it.

1041
01:36:33,760 --> 01:36:37,519
Whenever you work with me..

1042
01:36:38,920 --> 01:36:42,839
...whenever you decide to follow me...

1043
01:36:43,080 --> 01:36:44,479
...then you'll wear it.

1044
01:36:46,960 --> 01:36:48,159
This necklace...

1045
01:36:48,880 --> 01:36:51,999
...is the sign of my treason of Osman Bey.

1046
01:36:53,080 --> 01:36:54,599
It's the sign of...

1047
01:36:55,320 --> 01:36:57,519
...your devotion to Karesi Bey.

1048
01:37:01,400 --> 01:37:06,719
I won't give you something
and take it back like Osman Bey.

1049
01:37:07,720 --> 01:37:10,679
I won't embarrass you...

1050
01:37:10,760 --> 01:37:13,199
...in front of Beys, like Osman Bey did.

1051
01:37:15,920 --> 01:37:18,159
Who is Osman?

1052
01:37:18,840 --> 01:37:21,879
I have thousands of Beys...

1053
01:37:21,880 --> 01:37:24,279
...under my rule, just like him.

1054
01:37:26,480 --> 01:37:27,679
I'm saying...

1055
01:37:28,120 --> 01:37:30,999
....you can be as strong as Osman Bey.

1056
01:37:35,760 --> 01:37:36,599
Now...

1057
01:37:37,400 --> 01:37:40,999
...I have a ceremony to attend.

1058
01:37:41,960 --> 01:37:42,719
Excuse me.

1059
01:38:34,520 --> 01:38:37,159
Commander Lucas. They killed the watchers.

1060
01:38:37,320 --> 01:38:38,839
Damn it.

1061
01:38:38,960 --> 01:38:41,159
-Those barbarians will die.
-No!

1062
01:38:41,560 --> 01:38:44,759
Arcadaius no. They're too many in number.

1063
01:38:45,240 --> 01:38:47,719
Osman will burn but not now.

1064
01:38:48,520 --> 01:38:51,799
Later. We have a wedding to get to.

1065
01:38:52,080 --> 01:38:52,999
Come on!

1066
01:39:06,000 --> 01:39:07,759
My Bey Lucas is getting away!

1067
01:39:09,320 --> 01:39:10,599
Let's follow them.

1068
01:39:10,600 --> 01:39:12,599
No! Let him go!

1069
01:39:13,280 --> 01:39:16,759
He told me about the poison first.

1070
01:39:17,120 --> 01:39:18,639
So I'll let him live this time.

1071
01:39:21,440 --> 01:39:24,879
Now he's going to attack like
a dog because of his anger.

1072
01:39:24,880 --> 01:39:26,279
Not only him.

1073
01:39:26,280 --> 01:39:28,679
Karesi Bey will want to get revenge too.

1074
01:39:28,680 --> 01:39:30,439
We poked a hive.

1075
01:39:30,440 --> 01:39:34,159
The struggle has ended with this bridge.

1076
01:39:34,160 --> 01:39:37,359
They can do their worst.

1077
01:39:38,360 --> 01:39:40,199
This is the...

1078
01:39:40,960 --> 01:39:44,119
...part that the two sides
are closest to each other.

1079
01:39:44,120 --> 01:39:46,159
-That's why...Boran.
-Yes my Bey?

1080
01:39:46,159 --> 01:39:49,779
You will place the flying fire (Greek fire)
here and on the other side.

1081
01:39:49,779 --> 01:39:52,049
They won't be able to
build a bridge here again.

1082
01:39:52,049 --> 01:39:53,639
As you wish my bey.

1083
01:40:01,160 --> 01:40:04,399
This way come on. Search everywhere.

1084
01:40:05,760 --> 01:40:08,359
Hide now, come on.

1085
01:40:21,560 --> 01:40:24,239
Look everywhere.

1086
01:40:26,040 --> 01:40:28,279
This is the third party
we came across today.

1087
01:40:28,291 --> 01:40:30,639
It's a miracle we didn't
get caught my Shahzade.

1088
01:40:30,640 --> 01:40:32,479
That lowlife Lucas...

1089
01:40:32,640 --> 01:40:35,519
He prepared well because he was scared.

1090
01:40:35,680 --> 01:40:38,719
But fear doesn't change destiny...

1091
01:40:50,840 --> 01:40:53,959
They covered all the forest, my Shahzade.

1092
01:40:54,480 --> 01:40:56,399
We know, Baysungur.

1093
01:40:56,400 --> 01:40:58,029
Tell me what it's looking like.

1094
01:40:58,029 --> 01:41:02,239
I don't know if it works in our favor but
the priest that will wed Holofira Hatun...

1095
01:41:02,240 --> 01:41:03,959
...is coming this way.

1096
01:41:04,400 --> 01:41:07,109
How is he coming? How many
people are there Baysungur?

1097
01:41:07,109 --> 01:41:08,479
A horse cart...

1098
01:41:08,480 --> 01:41:10,519
...and some guards.

1099
01:41:12,000 --> 01:41:13,439
Ilbay.

1100
01:41:13,440 --> 01:41:15,319
You take the road.

1101
01:41:15,480 --> 01:41:17,519
Saruca, Yusuf.

1102
01:41:17,520 --> 01:41:20,839
You take the front. Go now. Come on.

1103
01:41:21,160 --> 01:41:23,919
What do you have in mind my Shahzade?

1104
01:41:28,040 --> 01:41:30,839
Gonca, I made this myself.

1105
01:41:30,840 --> 01:41:33,719
You don't eat anything. At least eat this.

1106
01:41:33,760 --> 01:41:36,399
No thank you Ulgen, I won't eat it.

1107
01:41:40,160 --> 01:41:41,879
Of course she can't.

1108
01:41:41,880 --> 01:41:45,159
She lost her baby because of the infidels.

1109
01:41:47,720 --> 01:41:49,439
It's not easy.

1110
01:41:51,520 --> 01:41:53,519
She is the devil.

1111
01:41:53,520 --> 01:41:56,599
She put the poison in my tent too.

1112
01:41:58,400 --> 01:42:00,879
So they know us well.

1113
01:42:02,440 --> 01:42:05,239
The traitors are among us.

1114
01:42:05,960 --> 01:42:09,799
Who did she come here
with? A princess or something.

1115
01:42:10,160 --> 01:42:11,599
She might be involved too.

1116
01:42:11,600 --> 01:42:13,359
Hazal Hatun.

1117
01:42:15,800 --> 01:42:18,799
Daughter Holofira is innocent.

1118
01:42:19,520 --> 01:42:21,239
Watch your tongue.

1119
01:42:21,240 --> 01:42:22,799
So that...

1120
01:42:22,800 --> 01:42:26,119
...you don't make the same
mistake Begum Hatun made.

1121
01:42:29,120 --> 01:42:31,359
Here, eat it Hazal Hatun.

1122
01:42:31,560 --> 01:42:34,519
My Gonca couldn't, so you should.

1123
01:42:36,040 --> 01:42:38,039
So that you stay quiet.

1124
01:42:43,160 --> 01:42:45,119
It's very delicious.

1125
01:42:45,120 --> 01:42:47,039
Thank you for the food.

1126
01:42:48,240 --> 01:42:49,759
Bala Hatun.

1127
01:42:49,760 --> 01:42:51,759
You mentioned a daughter in law.

1128
01:42:51,760 --> 01:42:54,279
Who is she? Where is she from?

1129
01:42:54,440 --> 01:42:56,959
I'll tell you Hazal Hatun.

1130
01:43:00,040 --> 01:43:02,039
You know her well.

1131
01:43:02,880 --> 01:43:05,159
The one you called the devil.

1132
01:43:05,320 --> 01:43:06,959
The one you called an infidel.

1133
01:43:06,960 --> 01:43:08,719
The one who...

1134
01:43:08,880 --> 01:43:11,119
...brought Cecillia into our tribe.

1135
01:43:12,880 --> 01:43:14,839
Holofira.

1136
01:43:18,280 --> 01:43:19,639
Gonca.

1137
01:43:21,640 --> 01:43:23,239
Gonca.

1138
01:43:23,480 --> 01:43:25,359
Daughter.

1139
01:43:26,160 --> 01:43:27,679
Let's talk.

1140
01:43:27,680 --> 01:43:28,689
Mother.

1141
01:43:29,200 --> 01:43:30,719
Not now.

1142
01:43:31,400 --> 01:43:33,199
Not now mother.

1143
01:43:33,760 --> 01:43:35,719
But know this.

1144
01:43:36,640 --> 01:43:38,679
If Holofira comes...

1145
01:43:39,080 --> 01:43:40,679
...then I'll leave.

1146
01:43:54,240 --> 01:43:56,399
What will we do Bala?

1147
01:43:57,040 --> 01:43:59,719
She's turning her pain into rage, Ulgen.

1148
01:44:00,400 --> 01:44:02,679
Keep your eyes on her.

1149
01:44:02,680 --> 01:44:05,199
Tough days are coming.

1150
01:44:20,640 --> 01:44:22,479
Be ready.

1151
01:44:35,040 --> 01:44:36,319
Wait.

1152
01:44:41,120 --> 01:44:42,679
Wait.

1153
01:44:49,320 --> 01:44:50,799
Now!

1154
01:44:50,800 --> 01:44:53,239
Allah is Everlasting!

1155
01:44:54,960 --> 01:44:56,519
Come on!

1156
01:44:57,800 --> 01:44:59,199
Come on!

1157
01:45:27,720 --> 01:45:30,199
Peace be with you, priest!

1158
01:45:31,000 --> 01:45:32,799
Who are you?

1159
01:45:41,640 --> 01:45:43,599
Tie the priest and get ready.

1160
01:45:43,600 --> 01:45:45,999
We will hit the road.

1161
01:45:46,760 --> 01:45:48,239
My shahzade.

1162
01:45:51,080 --> 01:45:52,879
It's not because I am afraid.

1163
01:45:53,320 --> 01:45:55,159
But how are...

1164
01:45:55,160 --> 01:45:58,199
...we going to attack a place
guarded by hundreds of soldiers?

1165
01:45:58,720 --> 01:46:02,399
Let's say we attacked.
How are we going to get out alive?

1166
01:46:02,419 --> 01:46:04,199
If you are afraid, stay back Saruca.

1167
01:46:04,200 --> 01:46:06,799
No, this is not fear.

1168
01:46:07,080 --> 01:46:08,559
It's caution.

1169
01:46:09,960 --> 01:46:11,599
We will go in there silently...

1170
01:46:12,600 --> 01:46:15,479
...and destroy everything to get out.

1171
01:46:16,840 --> 01:46:18,999
How is that possible my shahzade?

1172
01:46:19,560 --> 01:46:21,439
It will be possible.

1173
01:46:21,440 --> 01:46:23,559
It will be.

1174
01:46:24,040 --> 01:46:29,159
Now gather all the
dried herbs in the forest.

1175
01:46:29,480 --> 01:46:31,479
As you command my Bey.

1176
01:46:37,800 --> 01:46:40,679
My shahzade, what are we
going to do with the priest?

1177
01:47:24,800 --> 01:47:26,879
Beautiful Holofira.

1178
01:47:28,960 --> 01:47:30,599
Look at me.

1179
01:47:35,160 --> 01:47:36,759
Look at me!

1180
01:47:44,440 --> 01:47:47,639
In a moment, you will be my wife.

1181
01:47:47,880 --> 01:47:51,839
You will love this man
with whom you will spend...

1182
01:47:52,080 --> 01:47:54,079
...your life!

1183
01:47:54,840 --> 01:47:56,799
Smile a little.

1184
01:48:10,600 --> 01:48:13,799
Commander Lucas, Karesi Bey is here.

1185
01:48:13,800 --> 01:48:15,159
Let him come.

1186
01:48:33,840 --> 01:48:35,319
Karesi Bey.

1187
01:48:35,840 --> 01:48:37,319
You honored us.

1188
01:48:37,760 --> 01:48:39,789
I am not here for the wedding.

1189
01:48:40,080 --> 01:48:42,639
I am here to get information!

1190
01:48:43,760 --> 01:48:45,439
The relics were...

1191
01:48:46,280 --> 01:48:47,879
...taken by Osman.

1192
01:48:48,400 --> 01:48:51,599
The bridge was destroyed by Osman.

1193
01:48:52,800 --> 01:48:57,199
Now what's your plan, Lucas?

1194
01:49:09,480 --> 01:49:14,679
We sometimes win, sometimes lose.

1195
01:49:15,200 --> 01:49:18,039
You will either stay here and cry...

1196
01:49:18,720 --> 01:49:23,679
...or we will make a plan
together and finish Osman.

1197
01:49:25,880 --> 01:49:27,799
You choose, Karesi Bey.

1198
01:49:43,480 --> 01:49:45,599
Who's that coming?

1199
01:49:45,840 --> 01:49:47,479
One of our Alps my Bey.

1200
01:49:50,480 --> 01:49:51,279
Soldier.

1201
01:49:52,000 --> 01:49:53,039
What's the rush?

1202
01:49:54,000 --> 01:49:56,399
My Bey. Bala Hatun sent it.

1203
01:50:09,000 --> 01:50:09,839
Orhan.

1204
01:50:10,480 --> 01:50:12,389
What happened to my brother, father?

1205
01:50:13,600 --> 01:50:14,879
Lucas.

1206
01:50:15,960 --> 01:50:18,679
He's forcing Holofira to marry.

1207
01:50:19,720 --> 01:50:23,999
Orhan took a few Alps
and went to the Monk Mountain.

1208
01:50:27,360 --> 01:50:28,999
Saruca and Yusuf are with him.

1209
01:50:29,520 --> 01:50:31,079
Good boy.

1210
01:50:31,520 --> 01:50:33,799
He didn't leave Shehzade alone.

1211
01:50:33,800 --> 01:50:35,199
But Lucas...

1212
01:50:35,880 --> 01:50:37,639
He'll have an army ready.

1213
01:50:39,560 --> 01:50:41,399
Even if they save Holofira..

1214
01:50:42,320 --> 01:50:44,409
...they won't leave there alive.

1215
01:50:47,800 --> 01:50:49,459
What will we do Osman Bey?

1216
01:50:52,720 --> 01:50:56,519
Of course we'll go there,
and save them from infidels.

1217
01:50:57,000 --> 01:50:58,329
Come on.

1218
01:51:11,000 --> 01:51:12,959
Give me patience, my Allah!

1219
01:51:36,200 --> 01:51:37,039
Shehzade.

1220
01:51:38,080 --> 01:51:39,759
Karesi Bey is here.

1221
01:51:45,320 --> 01:51:46,679
When my Bey hears this..

1222
01:51:48,320 --> 01:51:50,439
...he'll go mad.

1223
01:51:55,440 --> 01:51:56,439
In the name of Allah.

1224
01:52:51,000 --> 01:52:53,359
Commander Lucas. The Priest is here.

1225
01:52:55,000 --> 01:52:55,919
Priest is here.

1226
01:52:56,920 --> 01:52:57,719
Get up.

1227
01:53:19,960 --> 01:53:23,119
Give me your hand or you'll crawl!

1228
01:53:37,160 --> 01:53:40,559
The sacred Priest is here.

1229
01:53:46,480 --> 01:53:47,599
Holofira.

1230
01:53:48,040 --> 01:53:49,399
Acadeius.

1231
01:53:50,200 --> 01:53:51,399
Step forward.

1232
01:53:53,520 --> 01:53:54,599
Step forward...

1233
01:53:56,320 --> 01:54:00,599
...so that your union can
be blessed with holy oath.

1234
01:54:01,160 --> 01:54:02,959
Ameen.

1235
01:54:05,400 --> 01:54:08,119
Welcome Great Father.

1236
01:54:08,560 --> 01:54:09,599
You honor us.

1237
01:54:16,760 --> 01:54:19,919
This couple who loves
each other passionately...

1238
01:54:20,280 --> 01:54:24,359
...will soon swear holy oaths...

1239
01:54:24,760 --> 01:54:26,839
...in front of the father.

1240
01:54:26,840 --> 01:54:31,039
May god give them a good future...

1241
01:54:31,480 --> 01:54:34,039
...and loyal children.

1242
01:54:34,040 --> 01:54:36,279
-Ameen.
-Ameen.

1243
01:54:50,800 --> 01:54:53,199
We're ready father.

1244
01:54:53,600 --> 01:54:55,959
You can start the ceremony.

1245
01:55:12,960 --> 01:55:15,399
I'm talking to you, father.

1246
01:55:15,560 --> 01:55:17,439
You can start.

1247
01:55:31,360 --> 01:55:33,519
Have you swallowed your tongue, father?

1248
01:55:33,520 --> 01:55:35,319
Start it.

1249
01:55:35,400 --> 01:55:37,359
I didn't come here...

1250
01:55:38,280 --> 01:55:40,279
...to wed people...

1251
01:55:42,120 --> 01:55:44,279
...but to kill people.

1252
01:55:49,960 --> 01:55:51,039
Come on Holofira.

1253
01:55:51,040 --> 01:55:53,239
Allah.

1254
01:55:56,080 --> 01:55:57,719
Soldiers.

1255
01:56:00,760 --> 01:56:02,239
Allah.

1256
01:56:14,360 --> 01:56:16,879
Come on.

1257
01:56:18,800 --> 01:56:21,399
Soldiers.

1258
01:56:24,480 --> 01:56:26,279
Orhan.

1259
01:56:28,880 --> 01:56:31,479
You won't make it out alive from here.

1260
01:56:47,280 --> 01:56:48,559
Orhan.

1261
01:56:50,760 --> 01:56:52,639
Orhan.

1262
01:56:52,640 --> 01:56:54,799
Catch them you fools.

1263
01:56:57,520 --> 01:57:00,399
Arcedeus, take your men and follow them.

1264
01:57:00,560 --> 01:57:02,239
Kill them both.

1265
01:57:02,600 --> 01:57:06,079
Come on. I'm going to kill you.

1266
01:57:11,040 --> 01:57:14,519
How are things going in
Karadin, Begum Hatun?

1267
01:57:17,480 --> 01:57:20,159
There's no room for another mistake.

1268
01:57:20,320 --> 01:57:21,639
You know that, right?

1269
01:57:21,640 --> 01:57:23,959
I increased the precautions.

1270
01:57:23,960 --> 01:57:25,839
I've given everyone their duties.

1271
01:57:25,840 --> 01:57:28,439
Everything is going well, Bala Hatun.

1272
01:57:29,000 --> 01:57:30,239
Good.

1273
01:57:34,720 --> 01:57:37,079
You can be sure that...

1274
01:57:37,800 --> 01:57:39,479
..I will never..

1275
01:57:39,680 --> 01:57:42,759
...disappoint...

1276
01:57:43,400 --> 01:57:45,039
...Osman Bey.

1277
01:57:45,040 --> 01:57:47,239
If you do...

1278
01:57:47,240 --> 01:57:49,719
...we won't show mercy.

1279
01:57:56,360 --> 01:57:58,799
But you know what?

1280
01:58:00,560 --> 01:58:05,559
I like you being so sure of yourself.

1281
01:58:06,400 --> 01:58:07,759
But...

1282
01:58:07,760 --> 01:58:11,199
...that's the thing that makes
you do mistakes the most.

1283
01:58:11,280 --> 01:58:12,959
You were...

1284
01:58:12,960 --> 01:58:16,439
...so sure that Hazal Hatun was guilty.

1285
01:58:20,640 --> 01:58:25,319
Now, it's time for you to make
up for another mistake of yours.

1286
01:58:26,840 --> 01:58:30,319
You'll apologize to Hazal Hatun.

1287
01:58:33,560 --> 01:58:35,799
Ask me to do anything...

1288
01:58:36,080 --> 01:58:39,159
...but not this, Bala Hatun.

1289
01:58:40,960 --> 01:58:44,199
-I would never apologise from Hazal...
-I'm not asking.

1290
01:58:44,200 --> 01:58:45,839
Begum Hatun.

1291
01:58:46,480 --> 01:58:48,519
I'm giving you an order.

1292
01:58:54,040 --> 01:58:57,519
Are you going to go against my word now?

1293
01:59:09,760 --> 01:59:14,319
When the knights in the
castles get this message...

1294
01:59:14,400 --> 01:59:17,799
...they will surround the forest.

1295
01:59:50,440 --> 01:59:53,079
Orhan. You are wounded.

1296
01:59:53,240 --> 01:59:55,879
Orhan, stop!

1297
02:00:09,120 --> 02:00:12,439
Orhan, stop.

1298
02:00:20,000 --> 02:00:21,919
-Are you okay?
-I am okay.

1299
02:00:22,600 --> 02:00:25,919
Orhan, you are wounded,
we need to treat it.

1300
02:00:26,680 --> 02:00:28,519
It's okay.

1301
02:00:28,640 --> 02:00:30,679
It's okay, Holofira.

1302
02:00:31,640 --> 02:00:34,199
I got you out of there.

1303
02:00:35,040 --> 02:00:37,919
No wound can hurt me.

1304
02:00:37,920 --> 02:00:40,079
If you hadn't come...

1305
02:00:40,320 --> 02:00:43,639
-I was going to either kill that cruel Arcadeus...
-But...

1306
02:00:44,560 --> 02:00:46,759
...I came, Lord's daughter.

1307
02:00:47,040 --> 02:00:48,719
I am here.

1308
02:00:56,760 --> 02:00:58,719
My shahzade.

1309
02:00:59,760 --> 02:01:04,439
I don't know how, but we
need to get out of this forest.

1310
02:01:06,160 --> 02:01:08,359
We will, Baysungur.

1311
02:01:08,560 --> 02:01:10,759
We will get out and go to our tent.

1312
02:01:11,120 --> 02:01:12,839
Then...

1313
02:01:13,880 --> 02:01:17,119
...we will have a glorious wedding.

1314
02:01:22,280 --> 02:01:23,639
What's that?

1315
02:01:25,240 --> 02:01:27,479
There is smoke over the mountain.

1316
02:01:30,080 --> 02:01:32,079
Lucas.

1317
02:01:34,680 --> 02:01:37,239
He sends a signal to soldiers around.

1318
02:01:37,240 --> 02:01:38,719
They will corner us.

1319
02:01:39,440 --> 02:01:42,159
They will surround the
forest. We are cornered.

1320
02:01:42,280 --> 02:01:43,639
We will get out, Yusuf.

1321
02:01:43,960 --> 02:01:45,879
We will find a way.

1322
02:01:48,800 --> 02:01:51,519
...we will pave our own path!

1323
02:01:52,960 --> 02:01:55,759
Come on, to the horses.

1324
02:02:07,280 --> 02:02:10,279
Spread out! Find Orhan and Holofira

1325
02:02:10,480 --> 02:02:13,039
Come on, be quick!

1326
02:02:36,240 --> 02:02:39,199
Osman Bey is approaching
from North, my Bey.

1327
02:02:51,240 --> 02:02:55,079
My Bey, Osman Bey is
approaching from North.

1328
02:02:55,560 --> 02:02:58,599
So he is coming to save his shahzade.

1329
02:03:00,160 --> 02:03:02,639
Let him come.

1330
02:03:04,600 --> 02:03:07,679
Having feuds between us...

1331
02:03:07,680 --> 02:03:09,959
...harms our unity.

1332
02:03:15,920 --> 02:03:18,759
Begum Hatun thinks the same.

1333
02:03:20,200 --> 02:03:21,719
Right?

1334
02:03:23,160 --> 02:03:25,039
Yes.

1335
02:03:29,120 --> 02:03:31,999
I am glad that...

1336
02:03:32,600 --> 02:03:35,559
...you were freed, and
that you did not commit...

1337
02:03:35,720 --> 02:03:37,839
...such a treacherous deed.

1338
02:03:38,240 --> 02:03:42,519
-Yes, you really seem happy to me!
-Hazal Hatun.

1339
02:03:48,800 --> 02:03:52,239
I acted impulsive and accused you.

1340
02:03:53,760 --> 02:03:55,639
Forgive me.

1341
02:03:57,120 --> 02:03:59,599
It's not easy, Bala Hatun.

1342
02:03:59,840 --> 02:04:02,079
I almost died.

1343
02:04:06,520 --> 02:04:10,399
Forgiving is hard, I know.

1344
02:04:12,880 --> 02:04:15,639
Begum Hatun made a mistake.

1345
02:04:17,400 --> 02:04:18,759
I know it.

1346
02:04:19,360 --> 02:04:22,399
But people make mistakes.

1347
02:04:23,480 --> 02:04:25,199
She knows it.

1348
02:04:27,840 --> 02:04:32,039
Now, you must be the
bigger person Hazal Hatun.

1349
02:04:38,680 --> 02:04:40,679
Okay then Bala Hatun.

1350
02:04:40,920 --> 02:04:42,679
I'll be the bigger person.

1351
02:04:44,640 --> 02:04:45,919
This is for you.

1352
02:04:49,080 --> 02:04:50,039
I forgive you.

1353
02:04:56,800 --> 02:04:59,599
You did your best Hatuns.

1354
02:05:00,080 --> 02:05:01,639
Now you're excused.

1355
02:05:16,840 --> 02:05:20,999
That's how you are belittled Begum Hatun.

1356
02:05:32,720 --> 02:05:35,679
You act like you're
the mother of this state.

1357
02:05:36,840 --> 02:05:41,199
But I swear I'll take everything Bala.

1358
02:05:41,600 --> 02:05:42,839
Everything.

1359
02:05:43,840 --> 02:05:44,559
Your home...

1360
02:05:46,200 --> 02:05:47,519
..and your husband.

1361
02:06:06,320 --> 02:06:07,479
Shehzade.

1362
02:06:07,680 --> 02:06:09,959
We're surrounded by them.

1363
02:06:10,080 --> 02:06:11,759
They're too many in numbers.

1364
02:06:11,760 --> 02:06:13,319
We can't handle this many men.

1365
02:06:17,480 --> 02:06:20,639
Lucas thinks like the devil.

1366
02:06:21,000 --> 02:06:22,719
There will be more soldiers.

1367
02:06:23,320 --> 02:06:24,439
Over here.

1368
02:06:28,960 --> 02:06:29,999
Shehzade.

1369
02:06:30,680 --> 02:06:33,639
I'll escape them. You must leave.

1370
02:06:34,240 --> 02:06:35,599
What are you saying Ibrahim.

1371
02:06:35,600 --> 02:06:38,199
I'll ride my horse and
escape. They'll follow.

1372
02:06:38,360 --> 02:06:39,879
You can escape.

1373
02:06:39,880 --> 02:06:43,119
No. I won't let you risk your life alone.

1374
02:06:44,280 --> 02:06:45,399
Shehzade.

1375
02:06:45,720 --> 02:06:47,039
He won't be alone.

1376
02:06:47,920 --> 02:06:49,439
We'll go with him.

1377
02:06:49,680 --> 02:06:52,759
I'll go too.

1378
02:06:57,240 --> 02:06:58,839
Catch them.

1379
02:07:02,560 --> 02:07:04,039
They're coming.

1380
02:07:04,880 --> 02:07:05,719
Shehzade.

1381
02:07:06,600 --> 02:07:07,999
There's no other way.

1382
02:07:08,720 --> 02:07:10,679
Or we'll get caught.

1383
02:07:10,680 --> 02:07:12,679
Don't attack them.

1384
02:07:13,321 --> 02:07:16,360
We'll meet at Boz Valley after
the soldiers leave you alone.

1385
02:07:16,360 --> 02:07:17,399
Come on.

1386
02:07:17,399 --> 02:07:18,879
Don't worry, my shahzade.

1387
02:07:19,240 --> 02:07:20,679
We'll meet there.

1388
02:07:21,760 --> 02:07:23,079
Come on.

1389
02:07:24,440 --> 02:07:26,199
If Allah permits, we will.

1390
02:07:40,720 --> 02:07:42,039
Come here dastards!

1391
02:07:43,280 --> 02:07:44,999
They're getting away! Catch them!

1392
02:08:17,440 --> 02:08:18,389
Alps!

1393
02:08:20,000 --> 02:08:21,279
Shields!

1394
02:08:33,520 --> 02:08:35,839
Orhan's life is in danger.

1395
02:08:36,280 --> 02:08:37,719
They knew we were coming.

1396
02:08:37,720 --> 02:08:39,349
How is this possible my Bey?

1397
02:08:39,349 --> 02:08:40,999
No one knew we were coming.

1398
02:08:42,120 --> 02:08:43,599
Well, they know.

1399
02:08:44,680 --> 02:08:47,959
Treason's done in hiding
but it's revealed eventually.

1400
02:08:49,560 --> 02:08:52,639
We're too exposed. This isn't good.

1401
02:08:54,240 --> 02:08:55,519
Where are the archers?

1402
02:08:55,520 --> 02:08:57,079
Everywhere my Bey.

1403
02:08:57,120 --> 02:08:58,739
They're too many in number.

1404
02:09:05,920 --> 02:09:07,639
They can't make a move my Bey.

1405
02:09:08,360 --> 02:09:11,119
They believe that we have a lot of men.

1406
02:09:11,320 --> 02:09:16,439
You will pay for being stubborn Osman.

1407
02:09:23,440 --> 02:09:24,799
Kanyumaz.

1408
02:09:24,800 --> 02:09:25,639
My bey.

1409
02:09:25,640 --> 02:09:29,199
Tell the archers to fire
their arrows a bit further.

1410
02:09:29,200 --> 02:09:31,039
As you wish my bey.

1411
02:09:35,800 --> 02:09:40,679
My bey we have to get out of
the arrows'Tange or we'll be ruined.

1412
02:09:41,640 --> 02:09:43,079
Alps.

1413
02:09:43,080 --> 02:09:44,479
Retreat.

1414
02:09:44,480 --> 02:09:46,839
This way. Don't separate.

1415
02:09:46,960 --> 02:09:49,599
Go on then Osman.

1416
02:09:49,600 --> 02:09:52,319
You hurt me.

1417
02:09:52,320 --> 02:09:54,759
Now it's time for you to feel pain.

1418
02:09:54,760 --> 02:09:57,159
Alps.

1419
02:09:58,360 --> 02:10:00,839
They're coming from behind too. Alps!

1420
02:10:00,840 --> 02:10:04,359
Together, come on.

1421
02:10:59,360 --> 02:11:01,359
Holofira, go now.

1422
02:11:01,360 --> 02:11:04,519
-I won't leave, Orhan.
-Come on.

1423
02:11:04,520 --> 02:11:06,479
Then take this.

1424
02:11:08,120 --> 02:11:10,479
This is our fight.

1425
02:11:11,440 --> 02:11:13,679
Either we fight together...

1426
02:11:13,680 --> 02:11:16,039
...or we die side by side.

1427
02:11:31,560 --> 02:11:33,559
Don't be scared Holofira.

1428
02:11:33,680 --> 02:11:35,239
We'll make it out of here.

1429
02:11:35,240 --> 02:11:36,839
I'm not scared.

1430
02:11:39,080 --> 02:11:41,679
Kill them both. Attack.

1431
02:12:22,040 --> 02:12:23,759
Holofira.

1432
02:12:35,040 --> 02:12:37,559
Come on.

1433
02:12:40,960 --> 02:12:43,119
My bey, we're nearly out of range.

1434
02:12:43,120 --> 02:12:43,999
Come on.

1435
02:12:44,000 --> 02:12:47,559
Osman was fooled by my white beard.

1436
02:12:47,560 --> 02:12:50,279
He doesn't know it but...

1437
02:12:50,280 --> 02:12:52,399
...even if the wolf gets old...

1438
02:12:52,880 --> 02:12:56,079
...it never leaves its prey.

1439
02:13:32,800 --> 02:13:34,879
Come out and fight like men.

1440
02:13:34,880 --> 02:13:36,879
You cowards.

1441
02:13:43,360 --> 02:13:45,559
We are cornered here,
there is nowhere to go!

1442
02:13:45,680 --> 02:13:48,519
An oppressor doesn't need a dungeon!

1443
02:13:48,680 --> 02:13:52,199
I swear that l am going to make the ones
who did this to us pay!

1444
02:14:02,765 --> 02:14:14,115
Contact us at turkision@gmail.com